        "raw": "<p>I searched for this ruling and could not find it; my apologies if weak search-fu lead to a redundant posting.</p><p>The question, no details: Does Synaptic Interruption redirect an instance of 3 or more damage, or a total amount of three or more damage from a single card/character/power?</p><p>The wording on SI is:</p><p>&quot;If Tachyon would be dealt 3 or more damage from a single source, you may redirect that damage to a target of your choice and destroy this card.&quot;</p><p>What constitutes a &quot;source&quot;? My intuition says a source is an instance of damage, but it could be argued it&#39;s a card, power, or character that is the &quot;source.&quot;</p><p>As an example of what I&#39;m confused about: Tachyon has SI out, and is the target of a villain card effect that causes her to take 1 cold, 1 fire, and 1 lightning. Can she redirect this, as it is &quot;3 or more damage from one source&quot;? Or does she have to suck up that damage because no one instance (i.e., no one &quot;source&quot;) is 1 damage?</p><p>Thanks in advance!</p>",
